# AGENTS.md — VentureLab Factory OS doctrine

## THE ONE RULE
Nothing is real because an agent said it, a file exists, or a task moved to done.
A claim is accepted only when independently defined evidence and reproducible logged gates support it.

## Authority
- Factory OS DB is canonical lifecycle truth.
- Hermes Kanban is the default worker/operations adapter.
- Beads is an optional dependency/coding mirror.
- Workers cannot self-certify.
- Markdown is documentation, not evidence.

## Execution
Prefer deterministic code when sufficient.
Otherwise Factory OS selects an approved executor; Hermes is default.
HotSwap chooses model/provider routes under quality, cost, quota and policy constraints.
No model is globally hard-coded.

## Evidence
Every observation, artifact, decision, gate, release and outcome needs:
stable ID, timestamp, content hash and provenance where applicable.

## Safety
No secrets in prompts/logs/artifacts.
No unapproved external side effects.
Publication/deployment requires release gates.
No platform/account/policy circumvention.
